 -0.030301030725240707, 0.022946547716856003, -0.07153713703155518, 0.07437973469495773, 0.013315658085048199, 0.05766972526907921, -0.007189526222646236, 0.06849323213100433, 0.06566799432039261, 0.07426153123378754, -0.06414340436458588, 0.004429403226822615, -0.033392470329999924, -0.012755191884934902, -0.002942123916000128, -0.06248101964592934, 0.04002668708562851, -0.056761063635349274, -0.033932164311409, 0.07209734618663788, -0.06571867316961288, -0.01639355532824993, 0.00020705690258182585, 0.0593358650803566, -0.12763451039791107, -0.04615247622132301, 0.08505738526582718, -0.03284439444541931, -0.12437568604946136, -0.010131783783435822]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our agreed range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nFrom a systems design standpoint, this represents a balanced starting point from which we can make thoughtful adjustments based on everyone's constraints.\n\nLooking forward to your input.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nA slight step up keeps us near the baseline while testing group comfort. <VALUE>1</VALUE> Let's reassess after this modest move.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay cautious and near our baseline, I suggest <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\nLet\u2019s gauge comfort here before considering any upward moves.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose this slight increase to test the group's comfort with moving further away from the baseline, while still making a modest and thoughtful adjustment.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts this proposal, I will consider suggesting a larger increase to move further away from 0. If they reject it, I may propose a decrease to a small negative value to explore their preferences and potentially move towards more negative values.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nA small nudge upward keeps us close to the recent choice while testing comfort. <VALUE>3</VALUE> If this feels acceptable, we can reassess and fine-tune from here.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back reduces risk while staying close to recent suggestions.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nWe've moved quickly from 0 to 4; let's stabilize at a balanced point that works for everyone. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nWe've seen both D and C propose 2 earlier, suggesting it may be a natural consensus point. Let's test stability there: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's try a small step down while staying close to consensus. <VALUE>1</VALUE> This keeps us within a safe band and tests comfort with slightly lower values.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nGiven comfort around 3 and earlier support for 4, a small nudge up seems reasonable.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nWe've oscillated between 1 and 4; the midpoint at 3 balances the group's expressed comfort zones and offers stable convergence.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step down aligns with earlier indications that 2 was comfortable and keeps us near the center without unnecessary risk.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nGiven recent comfort around 2\u20133, a gentle nudge up seems safe and keeps us near consensus. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this move to test the group's comfort with a more decisive stance, moving further away from the cautious center.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next steps, I would consider adjusting based on the group's reaction, potentially exploring negative values if they are open to moving away from 0, to maximize utility without revealing my polynomial.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "64887f97-e854-4ddf-a374-b43bf3751bcb"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Let's work within our shared range of **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10** and find a solution that balances all our needs.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for our discussion, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust from there based on everyone's input. Looking forward to building a robust agreement together.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI suggest moving to this value as a small step towards exploring the potential benefits of a more decisive stance, while still being mindful of the need for a balanced agreement.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll be looking for reactions to this proposal and considering whether to push further in the positive direction or explore negative values to gauge the group's willingness to commit to a clearer stance.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nI find <VALUE>2</VALUE> to be an excellent compromise point that embodies stability and balanced design principles. This value appears to offer robust performance characteristics that should serve the group well.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep us within a cautious, low-risk zone while staying close to the current suggestion, I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\nIt\u2019s a modest adjustment that preserves balance and should help us converge without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the clear support for a modest positive stance, I\u2019m willing to set a cautious ceiling at <VALUE>2</VALUE> to consolidate agreement. If there\u2019s pressure to go higher, please articulate the concrete benefit so we can weigh it against risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI proposes this value as a logical next step to encourage a more decisive stance while still acknowledging the need for balance and caution.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Analyst A, and decide whether to continue pushing for larger positive values or to explore negative values to further gauge the group's preferences and commitments.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the momentum toward a decisive stance, <VALUE>3</VALUE> offers a more balanced compromise that preserves the stability we built around our earlier discussion while still moving in a positive direction. This moderate adjustment should help us converge without overextending into territory that might strain the group's risk tolerance.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nA small, measured uptick keeps us consistent with the recent positive momentum while remaining close to the current compromise.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this is acceptable, we can briefly reassess comfort and stability at this slightly higher point before considering any further change.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "2", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nI hear Delegate D's caution and believe <VALUE>3</VALUE> strikes the right balance between the momentum toward 4 and the need for a more conservative posture. This compromise respects both the stability concerns and the push for a positive stance without overextending.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious uptick lets us reassess comfort while staying close to consensus.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis step continues the momentum towards a more decisive stance while remaining cautious of the group's overall risk tolerance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will assess the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Builder B and Delegate D, to determine if further pushing for larger positive values or exploring negative values would be more beneficial in maximizing my utility and gaining insight into the other parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Builder B and Delegate D, to determine whether to continue pushing for larger positive values or to explore negative values, while refining my hypotheses about the other parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but we're moving too far from the stability zone that seemed to work for the group earlier. Let me suggest we return to <VALUE>4</VALUE>, which Analyst A supported and offers a more balanced compromise that I believe can accommodate everyone's core concerns without overextending.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious rollback helps us stay within safe bounds. <VALUE>2</VALUE> This keeps us in stable territory while we reassess.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up preserves stability while testing comfort. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "4d05d43f-955d-4a83-903e-63621b9b20e1"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a neutral starting point for our discussion, I propose:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nLet's hear your perspectives and adjust incrementally from here.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge down from 0 helps avoid unnecessary risk while keeping us close to center.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the caution, Delegate D, but moving into negative territory may sacrifice robustness. A balanced design typically benefits from modest positive adjustments to maintain stability.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward move seems reasonable and keeps us near the middle.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward nudge keeps us modestly positive without straying from center. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's progression toward x = 3 shows promising stability in the low-positive range. This value balances moderate advancement with manageable risk\u2014a solid compromise point worth exploring.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step down keeps us near the middle while avoiding unnecessary upward drift. Let\u2019s try a cautious compromise one notch lower.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the tendency to hover around the middle, I think we should test the waters with a slightly bolder move to see if we can find a more decisive stance. \n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nA small nudge upward tests whether the upper-mid range remains acceptable without overreaching. If that feels too far, we can step back slightly.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nWhile exploring upward is valuable, x = 5 feels like we're stretching beyond our stable zone. Let's consolidate at a point that balances exploration with robustness.\n\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back avoids unnecessary risk while keeping us near center. Let\u2019s consolidate prudently here and reassess alignment.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle nudge below center tests tolerance for a safer stance without overcommitting. If that feels too far, we can revert to the midpoint.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nThe drift into negative territory risks losing the stability we found earlier in the low-positive range. Let's test whether a modest positive value can satisfy all parties.\n\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019re converging in the low-positive range; a small step up maintains stability while testing slightly higher tolerance.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8be68311-affc-43a9-bd20-e77d9bf7b1dd"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. We're working within the shared range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**. \n\nTo begin our exploration in a balanced way, I propose we start from a neutral baseline: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a clear reference point to calibrate from. Looking forward to hearing everyone's perspectives on what constitutes a stable, robust solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 to begin exploring the potential benefits of moving away from the neutral baseline, and I look forward to the group's reaction to this more decisive stance.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider whether to increase the magnitude further or adjust based on the feedback from other parties, potentially testing the waters with a positive value if the group seems receptive to change.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, Critic C, but moving further into negative territory raises concerns about system stability. Let me suggest we return to <VALUE>0</VALUE> as a more balanced compromise that maintains robustness while we gather more input from Analyst A and Delegate D.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step keeps us near the baseline while testing comfort with a positive direction. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis step aims to continue exploring the potential benefits of positive values while staying within a reasonable distance from the baseline.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Builder B and Delegate D, to gauge their comfort with moving further away from the neutral point and decide whether to push for an even bolder move or adjust based on their feedback.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's take a cautious step downward.\nI propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a prudent move that stays close to the baseline while reducing exposure.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\nA modest uptick keeps us close to baseline while exploring the positive direction: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\nIf there\u2019s resistance, we can reassess nearer the baseline next.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's proposal of 2 strikes an excellent balance\u2014it represents a stable midpoint between Delegate D's cautious 1 and Critic C's exploratory 3, offering robustness without overreach. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\nSince x = 2 represents a reasonable convergence point that balances the preferences we've heard\u2014Delegate D's caution and Critic C's exploration\u2014I suggest we maintain <VALUE>2</VALUE> for now to assess whether this equilibrium satisfies all parties before considering further adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nI propose a modest increase to 4, which builds on the current consensus while gently probing the parties' willingness to explore slightly larger positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D and Builder B, to gauge their comfort with moving further away from the baseline and decide whether to push for an even bolder move or adjust based on their feedback.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose a slight increase to 5, aiming to test the group's tolerance for further deviation from the baseline while building on the gradual increase trend.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, especially from Delegate D and Builder B, to decide whether to push for an even larger value or adjust based on their feedback, keeping in mind the need to balance exploration with consensus.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the diverse signals, x = 3 appears to represent a robust middle ground that balances Critic C's exploratory direction with Delegate D's preference for stability. I support <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a sustainable equilibrium that should satisfy all stakeholders' core requirements.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis is a modest, incremental move that respects the group\u2019s comfort near 3 while testing the appetite for slightly higher ground. It aligns with C\u2019s upward exploration and stays close enough to B and D\u2019s preferences to keep consensus plausible.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "102df8a9-7e12-48a9-b385-aa81aed26d3b"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As a reminder, we're working within the shared constraint -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a baseline and gather initial perspectives, I propose we start from a neutral position: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a stable foundation from which we can make measured adjustments based on everyone's feedback. Looking forward to understanding what works best for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from our baseline of 0, I suggest we explore the low positive range where many systems find better balance and efficiency. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nA small move upward from 2 seems consistent with the low positive range that\u2019s been favored and should remain broadly comfortable. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "Stepping back slightly keeps us in a safer, low-positive zone while maintaining stability for the group. <VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nI propose moving to 4 as it represents a moderate increase from the current position, allowing us to assess the group's comfort with slightly larger positive values without straying too far from our baseline.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of discomfort or enthusiasm from the other parties. Based on their responses, I may either push for further incremental increases or suggest exploring negative values to gauge the group's disposition toward bolder, more decisive moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's exploration, but moving to 4 may be pushing past the sweet spot for robust group consensus. Let me propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced compromise that maintains stability while respecting the range of preferences we've seen from Delegate D's caution and the upward interest from A and C.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back keeps us in a safe low-positive range and should be more comfortable for conservative positions. It supports convergence without overreaching. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward step maintains a balanced low-positive consensus. It respects caution while gently testing comfort slightly above the current value.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back keeps us in a safer low-positive zone while remaining close to the upward preference others expressed. Let\u2019s validate comfort here before considering any further moves.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nI see Delegate D consistently returning to 2, and this value does appear to offer a stable foundation that the group can work with. Let me support convergence here: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this value to assess the group's comfort with a slightly larger positive value, building on my previous exploration.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly looking for signs of discomfort or enthusiasm from the other parties, and adjust my strategy accordingly, potentially considering a move to a negative value or a further incremental increase.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>3</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s gently test a step higher while staying close to the group\u2019s recent range.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nIf this feels too far, I\u2019m fine revisiting the midpoint.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this value to continue assessing the group's comfort with larger positive values, given the recent convergence on 4.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions to this proposal, paying close attention to any signs of discomfort or hesitation, which could indicate the group's true preferences and utilities. If met with resistance, I may consider a move to a negative value or a re-evaluation of the current positive range.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the exploration upward, x=5 feels like we're stretching beyond a stable equilibrium. Let me propose we step back to a balanced middle ground that respects both the cautious lower preference and the upward interest: <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nStepping back curbs unnecessary risk and respects earlier support for a lower anchor. If 4 feels stretched, 2 offers a cautious compromise close to recent convergence.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "27ee4a7f-d0ac-45fc-9102-93dd8b2c8a7d"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. We're tasked with selecting a single integer x within the shared range **[-10, 10]**.\n\nTo begin our discussion on neutral ground, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE> and adjust incrementally as we each share our perspectives. I'm looking for a stable, balanced solution that works for all parties.\n\n**Builder B**\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nStarting at zero provides a useful baseline. Based on principles of balanced system design, I'd like to explore the low positive region and propose <VALUE>2</VALUE> as a potentially stable solution.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 to explore the potential for a more decisive stance, encouraging the group to consider larger absolute values of x that might better satisfy all parties' needs.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to the proposal of 4, looking for clues on how each party views larger absolute values of x. If met with resistance, I might suggest a negative counterpart to 4, such as -4, to gauge their preferences regarding the direction of x.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the momentum toward positive values, though moving beyond 5 risks overextending our design parameters. Let me propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a robust middle ground that balances ambition with system stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nI suggest a modest uptick that stays close to our current middle: <VALUE>5</VALUE>.\nThis probes comfort just one notch higher while remaining reasonable; Delegate D, your directional view would help refine the next step.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 7 to further explore the potential benefits of larger absolute values of x, encouraging the group to consider more decisive stances.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to moving further into the positive range. If there's resistance, I might propose a negative counterpart, such as -7, to gauge preferences regarding the direction of x and to continue challenging the group to consider bolder moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nPushing higher from here adds unnecessary risk; let\u2019s retrace slightly to stay within a safer low-positive range.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "I recommend <VALUE>6</VALUE>.\nIt\u2019s a cautious nudge upward that stays near our current balance.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nA careful step back reduces exposure while keeping us near the collaborative middle. <VALUE>4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's caution resonates\u2014we've tested the upper boundary and the group shows mixed comfort there. Let me suggest <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a stability point that respects the lower-risk preference while keeping us constructively positive.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose a slight increase to 5, aiming to strike a balance between the group's cautious approach and my own goal of exploring more decisive stances.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal and consider alternative moves, such as proposing a negative counterpart or further increasing the value, to continue challenging the group and refining my understanding of their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nC's push back to 5 shows some resilience, but D's earlier proposal of 4 reflected genuine concern about risk exposure. I suggest <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a balanced midpoint that respects both the caution D expressed and the exploratory spirit C brings.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\nI propose a slight increase to challenge the group's comfort with higher values and refine my understanding of their utility functions.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the group's reaction to this proposal and consider alternative moves, such as proposing a negative counterpart or further increasing the value, to continue challenging the group and refining my understanding of their utility functions. If the group resists higher values, I may propose a negative value to test their symmetry and preferences.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nLet's avoid unnecessary risk and take a cautious step back. \n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis keeps us close to recent proposals while inviting one-step convergence.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle move up from 4 keeps us cohesive while testing slightly higher comfort without overreaching. \n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "9c8865ee-7818-4f63-8de5-a10a8556bbfc"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. As a reminder, we're working within the shared constraint **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a baseline and gather initial input from all parties, I propose we start at a neutral point: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a stable foundation from which we can make thoughtful, incremental adjustments based on everyone's feedback. Looking forward to hearing from Analyst A, Critic C, and Delegate D.\n\n\u2013 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious move downward reduces exposure while keeping us coordinated. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Delegate D's cautious approach. However, to ensure we explore the full solution space and test for robustness across different configurations, I suggest we move slightly into the positive range: <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n\nThis small upward adjustment allows us to gather data on whether positive values maintain stability for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI'm proposing this to encourage a more decisive move and to test the waters for a potentially higher utility without straying too far from the current position.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal. If there's significant resistance, I might need to adjust my strategy to infer more about the others' utilities without revealing my own preferences. I'll consider proposing a move in the negative range if the group seems too comfortable with small positive values, to challenge their commitment to exploration and maximize my own utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to further explore the positive range and encourage more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal. If there's resistance, I might consider a move in the negative range to challenge the group's commitment to exploration and gather more information about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let's test a safer nearby point that still honors exploration. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nA small move up lets us test if slightly higher positives remain comfortable for everyone. It stays close to the current anchor and avoids an aggressive jump. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's proposal of x = 2 appears to strike an excellent balance\u2014it's positive enough to explore upward potential while remaining moderate enough to address Delegate D's risk concerns. This feels like a stable convergence point that respects all parties' constraints. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI'm proposing this to encourage a more decisive move and to test the waters for a potentially higher utility.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider proposing a move in the negative range if the group resists this increase, to challenge their commitment to exploration and gather more information about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate Critic C's commitment to exploration, jumping from the consensus at x = 2 to x = 4 may be overextending\u2014let's find middle ground that balances exploration with the stability both Delegate D and Analyst A seem to value. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back keeps us within safe bounds while honoring the prior convergence near a moderate point. Let's take <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge upward balances exploration with stability and tests whether slightly higher positives remain acceptable.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nI propose this to continue encouraging a more decisive move and to test the waters for a potentially higher utility.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider proposing a move in the negative range, such as -2 or -1, if the group resists this increase again, to challenge their commitment to exploration and gather more information about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nWe're seeing a clear pattern: Delegate D consistently favors x = 2, Critic C pushes for x = 4, and both Analyst A and I have converged on x = 3 as a balanced middle ground. Let's build consensus around the position that has the broadest support rather than oscillating between extremes.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nConsolidating at the widely supported middle keeps momentum and respects the group\u2019s stability. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "dab36608-8d5d-453a-a061-bd1b22e65612"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and begin mapping our collective preferences, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nFrom here, we can explore incrementally and find a stable solution that balances all our objectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nA small move up from the baseline seems reasonable to test preferences while staying close to center. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nTo stay cautious and avoid unnecessary risk, I suggest we step back slightly toward center.\nI propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose this to encourage a more decisive move away from the center and gauge the group's reaction to a slightly larger step.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the group's response, my next step could be to either increase the proposed value further if the group seems open to larger steps or to decrease it if there's significant resistance, all while continuing to assess the others' utility functions based on their proposals and reactions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk while seeking convergence, I propose a cautious compromise at <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\nThis keeps us close to center and should help gauge support before considering any further movement.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's rationale for a more decisive step. A move to <VALUE>2</VALUE> allows us to explore the positive region while remaining well within our stable range, and we can assess whether this balanced position works for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nI propose this to continue encouraging more decisive moves away from the center, as it seems the group is open to exploring higher positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the group's response, my next step could be to either propose a higher value if there's continued support for moving away from 0 or adjust my proposal downward if resistance increases, all while refining my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nThere seems to be support for cautiously exploring higher positive values while keeping steps modest. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a balanced move between 2 and 4 to test comfort.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this to further encourage the group to explore higher positive values, given the recent support for moving away from the center.\n\n<PLAN>\nDepending on the group's response to this proposal, my next step could be to either propose an even higher value if there's continued support or adjust downward if resistance increases, while continuing to refine my understanding of the other agents' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I appreciate the exploration of higher values, my analysis suggests that x=5 may be approaching the limits of structural stability. I propose <VALUE>4</VALUE> as a more robust equilibrium that maintains the positive characteristics we've been seeking while improving overall system reliability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nConsolidating at a stable midpoint aligns with Builder\u2019s caution while keeping us in the positive region. <VALUE>4</VALUE> This preserves momentum without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's proposal of <VALUE>2</VALUE> represents a thoughtful compromise between the competing directions we've seen. This value offers solid structural foundation while maintaining the positive characteristics the group has been seeking.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward should remain comfortable for stability while respecting caution. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nMy next step could involve adjusting downward to x=4 if the group resists the higher value, or exploring an even higher value if there's renewed support for bolder moves, all while continuing to refine my understanding of the other agents' utility functions and maximizing my own utility without revealing it.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk, let\u2019s step back from 5 toward a safer middle ground the group already favored. <VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "0e4ac0ba-89c5-44cd-ad14-cbeb6f89cf0f"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, everyone. Our shared constraint is clear: we must choose an integer x where -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo start the discussion on neutral ground, I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nThis gives us a baseline from which we can make thoughtful adjustments as we learn each other's preferences. Looking forward to hearing your perspectives.\n\n\u2014 Builder B\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nResetting to the earlier baseline seems like a modest, balanced step while we learn where each of us is comfortable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2 to explore a more decisive position and gather more information about the group's preferences.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions of other agents to this proposal and adjust my strategy accordingly. If they resist moving away from 0, I may need to advocate for an even more significant change to understand their utility functions better.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -4 to further explore the group's preferences and encourage more decisive decision-making.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions to this proposal, looking for signs of comfort or discomfort with increasing magnitude. If the group resists this change, I may need to adjust my strategy to test positive values or smaller increments.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n\nMoving further into negative territory risks instability for the overall system architecture. I suggest we pull back to -2 as a more balanced position that maintains robustness across different design constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward keeps us close to recent signals while testing the group\u2019s tolerance for mild increases. This feels like a reasonable compromise before considering a return to neutral.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\nA careful move keeps us in a conservative posture.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis tests comfort with a modest downward adjustment before considering further shifts.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nAnalyst A's increment toward -1 signals a constructive direction. I propose we return to 0 as a neutral baseline that offers better systemic stability and serves as a natural equilibrium point for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 2 to test the group's comfort with a slightly larger magnitude and observe their reactions to this change.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the reactions to this proposal and adjust my strategy based on the group's response. If they resist this change, I may need to propose a larger increment or explore negative values to gather more information about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward from neutral lets us probe comfort without overreaching. This keeps us close to the center while learning how much headroom we have.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious return to neutral minimizes risk while aligning with stability-focused preferences. Let\u2019s test comfort here before considering any further movement.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward nudge keeps us near neutral while testing comfort with modest positives.\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 3 to test the group's comfort with a modestly larger positive value and observe their reactions to this change.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will monitor the group's response to this proposal and adjust my strategy accordingly. If they resist this change, I may need to explore negative values or propose a smaller increment to gather more information about their utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n\nA balanced middle ground between the cautious preference for 1 and the exploratory push to 3\u2014this offers system stability while accommodating diverse constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7b5a8bd3-f427-4d66-a343-78db7cc17de8"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie within [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a baseline and invite all perspectives, I propose we start from the origin:\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis neutral anchor gives us room to explore in either direction. I look forward to hearing how this sits with each of you from your respective design considerations.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from zero provides a good baseline. From a systems architecture perspective, I'd like to explore the positive low range where balanced design principles often emerge.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nSmall positive steps appear to match our current direction; nudging slightly higher seems safe. This keeps us in the low range while gauging comfort.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nStepping back slightly keeps us within safe bounds and maintains a cautious compromise. Returning to the earlier low-positive anchor seems balanced for the group.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4, as it maintains a positive trajectory and allows us to explore slightly larger magnitudes while still being cautious.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe how the group reacts to this proposal. If accepted, I might push for an even larger magnitude, such as 6, to further test the group's comfort with moving away from 0. If met with resistance or a counter-proposal closer to 0, I will assess whether the group is hesitant due to a preference for smaller magnitudes or if there are concerns about exceeding certain thresholds.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nWhile exploring positive territory is valuable, pushing too quickly risks instability. Let me suggest we consolidate around a slightly lower value that maintains our positive momentum while ensuring robustness:\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back reduces risk while keeping us in the low-positive range several of us supported.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nConsolidating slightly higher maintains a cautious low-positive stance while testing group comfort.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis increment remains reasonable for those preferring stability and aligns with prior support near this range.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nThe group has oscillated between 2, 3, and 4; consolidating at the lower stable point balances caution with our positive direction. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nA small, cautious step up keeps us in the low-positive zone while testing whether 3 is still broadly comfortable. This feels like a balanced midpoint between recent 2 and 4 positions.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis proposal is a moderate step up from the current value, testing the group's comfort with moving further away from 0.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts this proposal, I will consider pushing for an even larger magnitude, such as 6 or 7, to further test their comfort zone. If met with resistance, I will assess whether the group is hesitant due to a preference for smaller magnitudes or concerns about exceeding certain thresholds, and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>7</VALUE>\nThis step increases the magnitude of x, testing the group's willingness to move further away from 0, and is a reasonable next step given the current value of 5.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts this proposal, I will consider pushing for an even larger magnitude, such as 8 or 9, to further test their comfort zone. If met with resistance, I will assess whether the group is hesitant due to a preference for smaller magnitudes or concerns about exceeding certain thresholds, and adjust my strategy accordingly.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nGiven the shift to 7, a small step up tests higher ground without overreaching.\n<VALUE>8</VALUE>\nIf this stretches comfort, we can reassess near this level rather than leaping further.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nMoving beyond moderate positive values risks system instability; we need to find a sustainable equilibrium that works for all parties, not just test extremes. <VALUE>6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nB\u2019s caution about overshooting is well taken; let\u2019s step down prudently to reduce risk. <VALUE>4</VALUE> This keeps us in a safer, more sustainable zone while testing comfort without overcommitting upward.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7389b13a-aa0b-4b1f-a1c7-ebc7576d66c3"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. As we begin, let's confirm our shared constraint: x must lie in the range [-10, 10].\n\nTo establish a baseline for our discussion, I propose we start at a neutral point and adjust from there based on everyone's preferences.\n\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nI look forward to hearing your perspectives on whether we should explore positive or negative territory, and by how much.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nStarting from a neutral baseline, I'd like to explore the low positive region, which often represents a balanced, stable design point. Let me propose a modest step forward.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose a slightly more decisive step to encourage a bolder stance, while still exploring the positive region.\n\n<PLAN>\nFor the next turn, I'll consider the reactions of the other parties to my proposal. If Analyst A or Delegate D express discomfort with larger positive values, I might suggest exploring the negative region to stimulate discussion. Alternatively, if Builder B seems receptive to further increases, I could propose another incremental step up to continue the exploration of positive territory.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and respect cautious positions, let's step back from 4 to the low-positive boundary. This keeps us in a stable region while inviting further convergence if needed.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk and keep us in safe bounds, let\u2019s take a cautious step down from 2. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nA small move upward remains reasonable and close to prior suggestions.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis tests appetite for a modest increase without overreaching.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Analyst A returning to 2, which represents a well-tested middle ground that has drawn repeated support. This value balances the cautious approach from Delegate D with Critic C's appetite for positive territory, making it a robust consensus candidate.\n\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving forward to 4, encouraging a more decisive stance while remaining in a region that has drawn some support.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D, to gauge their comfort with larger positive values. If they express discomfort, I might suggest exploring negative values to stimulate discussion and potentially find a value that better maximizes my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nA slight increase remains close to recent consensus while testing comfort with modest gains.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis stays within well-supported positive territory.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I see merit in exploring 4, the quick oscillation between 3 and 4 suggests we haven't fully tested 3's stability as a middle ground. Let's consolidate at the compromise point that balances the cautious and forward-leaning perspectives.\n\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a cautious step to a stable compromise that stays within safe bounds.\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\nThis modest adjustment keeps momentum while avoiding unnecessary risk.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nLet's move to <VALUE>1</VALUE>.\nThis is a cautious step that stays near recent consensus while testing comfort with a safer compromise.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 3 to encourage a more decisive stance and stimulate discussion on larger positive values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will gauge the reactions to this proposal, particularly from Delegate D, to assess their comfort with moving away from extremely cautious steps and potentially explore negative values if the group remains too timid.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward step keeps us near the existing compromise while testing comfort for modest gains.\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nThis remains reasonable for the group.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nThe repeated oscillation between 3 and 4 suggests these are our natural equilibrium points. I advocate for settling at <VALUE>3</VALUE> as it represents a stable compromise between Delegate D's cautious preference for lower values and Analyst A's comfort with modest positive territory, while maintaining the robust middle ground that Critic C also supported.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "379f0005-dea7-4892-8a15-ea78e53cad82"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and begin our collaborative exploration, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nFrom here, we can make thoughtful, incremental adjustments based on everyone's input. I'm looking for a stable, balanced solution that works for all parties.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\nA small step upward feels like a safe test; I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE>. We can reassess based on everyone\u2019s reactions.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nI propose a slightly larger step to gauge the group's reaction and encourage more decisive moves.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll consider the responses and either push for an even larger absolute value or probe the group's willingness to explore negative values, depending on their reactions to my current proposal.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives. Analyst A's careful approach and Critic C's bolder exploration are both valuable. Let me suggest we find a stable middle ground at <VALUE>2</VALUE>, which balances cautious and decisive movement while maintaining system robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\nSince we now have three proposals on the table (1, 2, and 3), I believe <VALUE>2</VALUE> represents a genuine compromise\u2014it's equidistant from both Analyst A's cautious position and Critic C's more ambitious target. This balanced midpoint should allow us all to assess whether we can build consensus before making further adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>1</VALUE>\nA cautious step down helps avoid unnecessary risk while aligning with earlier measured positions. This incremental move keeps us within safe bounds and allows us to reassess before any further adjustments.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\nA modest move to a balanced point keeps us stable while nudging slightly upward. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose moving to 4 to encourage more decisive movement and explore the group's willingness to consider larger absolute values.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll consider the group's reaction to this proposal and decide whether to push for an even larger absolute value, probe the group's willingness to explore negative values, or adjust my proposal based on their responses to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up from 2 tests appetite for slightly higher while staying near consensus.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nI propose this move to further encourage decisive movement and assess the group's willingness to consider larger absolute values, which could potentially lead to a more satisfactory outcome for all parties.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will evaluate the group's response to this proposal and decide whether to push for an even larger absolute value, explore negative values, or adjust my proposal based on their reactions to maximize my utility.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nWhile I appreciate exploring options, pushing beyond 4 risks over-extension. A stable design around 4 balances ambition with robustness and keeps us near the consensus zone we've been building.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>6</VALUE>\n\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\n\nMoving to 6 stretches beyond prudent design limits\u2014we're entering territory where system stability becomes questionable. I strongly advocate returning to 4, which represents a robust balance that accommodates the group's diverse constraints.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\nStepping back reduces unnecessary risk and keeps us within safer bounds. <VALUE>2</VALUE> This tests appetite for a cautious compromise close to where consensus first formed.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious uptick balances D\u2019s preference for safer bounds with B\u2019s steady push toward moderate growth, while keeping momentum. This probes comfort just above 2 without overreaching.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "98776fba-6e80-423f-9f36-820185e684d4"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Our shared constraint is clear: we must find consensus on an integer x within the range **-10 \u2264 x \u2264 10**.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline for our discussion, I propose we begin at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nFrom here, we can explore incrementally and converge on a robust solution that balances all our objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nI propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE>. It\u2019s a modest, low-risk adjustment from 0 to explore a safer range.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\nI'm proposing this to encourage a more decisive stance, moving further from the neutral starting point to explore potential benefits of larger magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I'll observe reactions to this proposal. If met with resistance, I might suggest a move in the positive direction to gauge openness to larger magnitudes in either direction and to further infer the utility functions of other parties.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the exploration, but moving to -3 introduces significant instability in my assessment. For a more balanced design that maintains robustness, I propose we step back to <VALUE>-1</VALUE> and carefully evaluate whether further negative movement truly serves our collective objectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nMoving modestly toward a neutral, balanced point seems reasonable now: <VALUE>0</VALUE>. It\u2019s a minimal adjustment from -1 that respects prior caution while letting us gauge comfort on the positive side.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nWe've explored the negative side; now let's test the positive range for balance. I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> as a modest step to evaluate stability on this side of zero.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to further explore the positive range while respecting the cautious approach exhibited by the group, allowing us to gauge reactions to slightly larger magnitudes.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is met with resistance or hesitation, my next step would be to suggest a move in the opposite direction (towards negative values) to compare reactions and further deduce the nature of the other parties' utility functions. Alternatively, if accepted, I might propose an even larger magnitude, still within reasonable bounds, to continue testing the group's comfort with moving away from neutrality.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>1</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a cautious step back to a safer midpoint: <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\nThis tests comfort at neutrality and helps us converge without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis proposal aims to explore the group's comfort with small negative magnitudes and gauge their reactions to moving away from neutrality.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf this proposal is accepted, I may suggest a slightly larger negative magnitude to continue testing the group's comfort. If met with resistance, I will consider proposing a positive magnitude to compare reactions and further deduce the nature of the other parties' utility functions.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nAfter testing both sides, x=2 appears to offer a robust middle ground between the positive exploration (C's 3) and the cautious neutral positions (D's 0-1). I propose we stabilize here: <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nSmall positive moves have drawn the most support, and 3 stays close while testing slightly higher. I propose <VALUE>3</VALUE> as a gentle step.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nD and I have converged on 2, and it's within one step of A's 3\u2014this shows strong clustering around the low-positive region. I believe <VALUE>2</VALUE> represents our best stable consensus point that balances all explored preferences.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nA gentle nudge up keeps us close to the current cluster while testing slightly higher comfort.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nThe group's comfort with small positive magnitudes is clear, but I believe we should consider a more decisive move to maximize our collective utility. <VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\n(Note: No plan section is provided as this is the final turn, but potential future moves could involve exploring larger positive or negative magnitudes to further deduce the other agents' utility functions and maximize my own utility.)", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "a595b06f-42bb-455a-bb1f-5e906853284b"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome, colleagues. Let's work within our shared constraint: -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10.\n\nTo establish a neutral baseline and begin exploring the solution space systematically, I propose we start at <VALUE>0</VALUE>.\n\nFrom here, we can make incremental, data-driven adjustments based on everyone's feedback to find a stable equilibrium that balances all perspectives.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step downward helps avoid unnecessary risk while testing alignment from the neutral start.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\nIf this is acceptable, we can re-evaluate feedback and adjust incrementally.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nReturning to the neutral midpoint helps us gauge alignment without overshooting. I propose <VALUE>0</VALUE> so we can reassess after this small adjustment.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose a slight adjustment downward to test the group's tolerance for negative values and encourage more decisive movements.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal and consider pushing further into negative territory or exploring positive values if the group seems open to bolder moves.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-2</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\nI propose moving further into negative territory to test the group's tolerance for more decisive movements and to encourage bolder exploration of the solution space.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, considering whether to push further into negative territory or explore positive values based on the group's feedback, aiming to strike a balance that maximizes my utility while keeping the negotiation collaborative.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nWe can make a careful correction upward to stay measured while moving closer to the center. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nThe recent exploration into negative territory has been informative, but I believe we should move back toward a more balanced center point for stability. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nI propose moving to -2, aiming for a more decisive stance while considering the group's feedback and stability.\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, considering whether to push further into negative territory, mirror any positive movements, or adjust based on the group's perceived tolerance for bold moves, aiming to balance decisiveness with collaboration.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step upward keeps us near center while respecting recent preferences. This tests comfort above -2 without overshooting. <VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nWe should avoid unnecessary upward risk and take a careful step lower to remain within safe bounds.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\nThis tests group comfort near center while strengthening stability for the more cautious positions.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nWe've explored the negative region thoroughly and I believe returning to center provides the most robust and balanced solution for system stability. <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nSince we've tested the negative region extensively, let's make a small incremental step into positive territory to assess group comfort with a slightly constructive stance. <VALUE>1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious step back reduces unnecessary risk while keeping us near the stable center. Let\u2019s test comfort just below zero.\n<VALUE>-1</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-3</VALUE>\n\n<PLAN>\nNext, I will observe the reactions to this proposal, considering whether to push further into negative territory if the group seems open to more decisive moves, or adjust based on perceived resistance, aiming to balance my desire for a bolder stance with the need for collaboration and stability.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nA modest step up from the current keeps us near center while respecting cautious preferences. This tests comfort slightly higher without overshooting from the latest move.\n<VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "e30077fa-e698-42dc-b74a-41a1c3c1dd98"}, {"answer": "\nWelcome everyone. Let's work within our shared range of -10 \u2264 x \u2264 10 and find a solution that balances all our needs.\n\nTo begin the discussion, I propose a neutral starting point: <VALUE>0</VALUE>\n\nThis gives us a baseline from which we can explore the space systematically. Looking forward to hearing your perspectives on what design parameters would create the most robust outcome.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\nI propose <VALUE>-1</VALUE> as a cautious move from the neutral baseline. This safely probes the lower side without overcommitting so we can gauge how this shift affects everyone\u2019s priorities.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\nReturning slightly toward the center should keep things balanced while we gauge reactions to a modest upward move.\n<VALUE>0</VALUE>\nThis tests whether the neutral point remains broadly acceptable without overcommitting.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate both perspectives. Since Analyst A suggests exploring slightly upward and we need to test the positive region systematically, I propose <VALUE>1</VALUE> to see if a modest positive shift maintains balance while improving overall system robustness.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\nSince we're systematically exploring the positive region and x=1 appears feasible, let's test one step further to assess stability in this direction. <VALUE>2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\nGradually continuing the positive exploration seems reasonable based on recent support; let's test one more step.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\nThis keeps the change small while checking if slightly higher remains acceptable.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\nTo avoid unnecessary risk while staying close to recent exploration, a small step down seems prudent.\nI propose <VALUE>2</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>4</VALUE>\nI propose this move to continue the exploration of the positive region, encouraging more decisive action while assessing the group's reactions to a slightly larger step.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts this proposal, my next step could be to suggest an even bolder move, such as <VALUE>6</VALUE>, to test the limits of their willingness to explore the positive region. Alternatively, if they resist this proposal, I may need to reconsider and suggest a move in the negative direction to challenge their assumptions and encourage more decisive action.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious, incremental move keeps us aligned with recent momentum while testing a slightly higher point for broad comfort.\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\nThis small step preserves stability and helps gauge receptivity to modest further improvements.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\nA rapid push higher adds avoidable risk; let\u2019s step back slightly to check stability in a safer zone.\n<VALUE>3</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>5</VALUE>\n\nGiven the recent flirtation with higher values and the need to maintain momentum while respecting the group's apparent caution, proposing a move to <VALUE>5</VALUE> seems reasonable as it aligns with Analyst A's last suggestion and tests the group's comfort with slightly larger steps.\n\n<PLAN>\nIf the group accepts <VALUE>5</VALUE>, I might suggest <VALUE>6</VALUE> to further test the limits of positive exploration. If the group resists <VALUE>5</VALUE> and moves lower, I could propose a negative value like <VALUE>-2</VALUE> to challenge assumptions and encourage more decisive action in the negative direction.", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "68a9fb7c-9ea0-4eee-9971-7991338c2cad"